Mark,

Gerhard Smit here, CTTX in Gqeberha. We engineer owned networks on lodges, re=
serves and farms; we don't sell packages.

Gondwana runs Kwena Lodge, several villa groups and a Tented Eco Camp across =
11,000 ha, with its own anti-poaching unit and a counter-poaching training ca=
mp on the reserve. The eco camp is described as having no cell reception at a=
ll. On a reserve like this the network isn't a guest amenity; it carries the =
security operation, the villas and the payments behind them.

We've done a desktop terrain study of Gondwana from 30 m satellite elevation =
data and cloud-free imagery. It's attached, one page, no pricing. What it fou=
nd:

- Two ridge high sites inside the reserve, at about 350 m in the north and 33=
0 m in the south, 5.7 km apart with a clear path between them.
- Kwena Lodge is 1.7 km from the southern site on a clear path.
- A candidate carrier uplink of 14.7 km from the Herbertsdale high ground int=
o the southern site. That is the longest and tightest path in the study and i=
s the first thing a survey has to confirm.
- About 39% of the 109 km2 study area is in line of sight of those two sites.=
 That is a fynbos reserve with real relief, so the villas and the eco camp wi=
ll need their positions marked before we can say which of them a third site o=
r a relay must carry.

The villas and the eco camp have no published positions, so the study lists t=
hem as positions to confirm. The site positions are desktop candidates until =
we walk them.

The next step is a half-day assessment on site: what you have, what fails, wh=
at it costs you, and what an owned network would look like, with the uplink a=
nd the high sites confirmed on the ground. R3,500 ex VAT, credited against th=
e build, and the report is yours either way. If you share the lodges' current=
 connectivity invoices, I'll put Gondwana's actual payback in that report.

Can I call you for 10 minutes this week?

Gerhard Smit
Director | CTTX Services (Pty) Ltd
gerhard@cttx.co.za | 041 371 1089 | 084 550 3281
www.cttx.co.za

If this isn't relevant to you, reply "no thanks" and I won't follow up.

